        en: "CHROMATIN IS NOT A SYNONYM FOR DNA, AND THE WORD CHROMOSOME MEANS TWO DIFFERENT THINGS THAT ARE WORTH KEEPING APART. Lehninger opens by settling the vocabulary, and it is worth copying exactly because the exam will use both senses. A chromosome is (i) the nucleic acid molecule that is the repository of genetic information — in a virus, a bacterium, an archaeon, a eukaryotic cell or an organelle — and (ii) the densely coloured bodies seen down a light microscope in dye-stained nuclei during mitosis. Between divisions the two senses do not look alike at all. In G0 and throughout interphase (G1, S, G2) “ the chromosomal material ” is amorphous — there are no visible chromosomes (A p.898). DNA replicates during S phase, each chromosome producing two sister chromosomes, called sister chromatids, that stay associated after replication finishes; only at prophase of mitosis does the material condense into the species-specific number of well-defined pairs you can photograph (Fig. 24-22, A p.899). The material itself, chromatin, is fibres of protein and DNA in approximately equal proportions BY MASS, plus a significant amount of associated RNA — and that RNA is not a contaminant, it is a genuine structural component, which the section returns to later.",
        cn: "**染色质不是 DNA 的同义词，而「染色体」这个词有两个值得分清的含义。** Lehninger 开篇先把词定下来，值得照抄，因为考试两种含义都会用。染色体是：(i) 承载遗传信息的**核酸分子**——在病毒、细菌、古菌、真核细胞或细胞器中；以及 (ii) 有丝分裂时，染色后的细胞核里用**光学显微镜**能看到的那些深染小体。两次分裂之间，这两个含义看上去完全不像。在 G0 期和整个间期（G1、S、G2），**染色体物质是无定形的**——根本看不到染色体（A 第 898 页）。DNA 在 **S 期**复制，每条染色体产生两条**姐妹染色体**，称为**姐妹染色单体 (sister chromatids)**，复制完成后仍彼此结合；只有到**有丝分裂前期**，这份物质才凝缩成物种特异数目的、界限分明的成对结构，也就是能拍下来的那种（图 24-22，A 第 899 页）。而这份物质本身——**染色质**——是蛋白与 DNA **按质量大致各半**的纤维，外加**相当量的 RNA**；这些 RNA 不是杂质，而是**真正的结构组分**，本节后面会再回来讲它。"
