          "Histone binding wraps DNA as a left-handed solenoidal supercoil, which introduces one negative supercoil per nucleosome; because binding breaks no strand, a compensating positive supercoil appears in the free DNA, and a topoisomerase then relaxes that positive one, leaving a net decrease of one in linking number",
          "Underwinding in eukaryotes is a purification artifact and does not exist inside the intact nucleus",
